// Sub-plan D fixture, unit B of the cross-unit staleness gate.
//
// Analyzed alone, `foreign` does not resolve, its call falls back to the
// language's preserving rule, and `wrapper` exports `Preserve` — so a caller
// keeps believing 16-bit after calling it. Analyzed with unit A visible,
// `foreign` is `Fixed(@a8)`, so `wrapper` *really* returns 8-bit. A summary
// taken before resolution is therefore not merely imprecise: every caller
// that consumed it sizes its immediates one byte too wide, and every byte
// after them shifts.
//
// The gate is that compiling this unit alone and compiling it with `--unit`
// naming A must not disagree about `wrapper`'s emitted code.

import "contract-unit-a.k816"

func wrapper @a16 {
    call foreign
}

func third @a16 {
    call wrapper
    lda #$01        // 8-bit: `wrapper` exits at whatever `foreign` left
}
